# Description:
# One window per group of related actions, so a dock cell that used to fire one
# fixed command becomes an icon that opens a real control surface.
#
#     kodachi-command-window tor-exit
#     kodachi-command-window tor-exclude
#
# Every window is a DEFINITION, not a new program: the shell, the row widgets
# and the whole visual language live in kodachi_ui, so the nineteenth window
# costs what the third one cost.
#
# Two things the cell grid could never do and this does:
#   - a control shows the state that IS, read before the window draws, rather
#     than the state you last asked for;
#   - nothing runs until Apply, every row carries the exact command it would
#     run as its tooltip, and the footer names the shape of what Apply does
#     it does, because a privacy tool that changes your routing silently is
#     worse than one that asks.
#
# Set KODACHI_DRY_RUN=1 to print the commands instead of running them.

